<title>FRANCE: Axa details main shareholdings.</title>
<headline>Axa details main shareholdings.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurance company AXA-UAP gave the following details on Wednesday of its main shareholdings, as of February 12, in percentages.</p>
<p>				    capital		  voting rights</p>
<p>Air Liquide...............   3.03		     3.04</p>
<p>Alcatel....			1.75		     1.62</p>
<p>BNP........		     12.05		    12.27</p>
<p>Credit National (Natexis)*   9.62		     9.20</p>
<p>Danone.....			3.9			4.11</p>
<p>Elf........			4.39		     4.56</p>
<p>Generale des Eaux.........   4.84		     5.47</p>
<p>Havas......			3.15		     3.15</p>
<p>Lyonnaise des Eaux........   5.41		     6.45</p>
<p>Paribas....			9.81		     5.25</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc.............   1.48		     1.27</p>
<p>Saint Gobain..............   4.74		     6.80</p>
<p>Schneider..			8.69		    12.90</p>
<p>Suez *.....			5.46		     7.74</p>
<p>NOTE - AXA sold its holdings in Suez on February 18 and in Credit National on February 20.</p>
<p>Earlier the French stock markets association, SBF, said in a statement AXA had proposed to allow its shares to go ex-dividend on May 14. AXA's 1996 results and dividend will be published on March 26.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
